# Sending a message again after the mesh came back to say it did not arrive.
#
# A failed bubble was drawable and nothing else: the error fill, the reason under it and the
# alert mark in the corner have been there since the transcript was written, and the only thing
# a reader could do about one was type the whole message out a second time. The phone apps let
# you tap it and resend, and this is that press.
#
# What the frames are for is the *keycap*, because that is the whole of the interaction and it
# is a property of the bubble rather than of the screen: START says "resend" while the cursor
# is on the message that failed and says nothing at all one line up, where there is nothing to
# send again. A keycap that appeared everywhere and worked on one row would be the action bar
# promising a press the nav refuses.
#
# The send itself is not here. There is no app behind this harness, so the MESH_UI_ACTION_RESEND
# the press raises goes nowhere - see docs/ui.md, and the `reply out` verb replies.scene uses to
# stand a send in.

scene demo
scale 4
clock 2026-01-12 19:12
tab messages

# Into the direct conversation with Bravo Creek.
key down 4
key a
hold 500

# One of ours, refused. Routing_Error 35 is PKI_UNKNOWN_PUBKEY - the reason goes under the
# message as a supporting line, and the mark in the corner is the same alert circle the
# delivery scene walks.
message out BRVO Bring the spare antenna
ack failed 35
hold 1600

# Up one, onto a message that arrived: the retry goes off the bar and START is back to standing
# in for A, which is what it does on every screen that has not spent it.
key up
hold 1400

# And back down onto the refused one, where it returns.
key down
hold 1400

# The press, and then the held button. One press is one send: START raises the retry and is
# spent, so the keycap goes at once rather than waiting for the store to catch up - which is
# what stops the kernel's autorepeat putting the same words on the air thirty times a second.
# The second press does nothing at all, and in particular does not fall through to A and open
# the compose sheet. Any other press re-arms it, which the `key up` below shows.
key start
hold 1400
key start
hold 1000
key up
hold 1200
